      <title>New Hampshire’s ‘bathroom bill’ vetoed for the third time</title>
      <link>https://www.nhpr.org/nh-news/2026-02-09/new-hampshire-nh-transgender-rights-ayotte-veto-bathroom-bill-politics</link>
      <description>The Republican-backed bill sought to create exceptions to the state’s antidiscrimination law, which protects people from discrimination on the basis of “gender identity” and other characteristics. Gov. Kelly Ayotte vetoed a nearly identical bill last year.</description>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">https://www.nhpr.org/nh-news/2026-02-09/new-hampshire-nh-transgender-rights-ayotte-veto-bathroom-bill-politics</guid>
